\dfrac{\textrm d}{\textrm d t}(\sinh t) = \cosh{t} \quad\Rightarrow\quad  \int \cosh{t} \, \textrm dt = \sinh{t} + C.
$$

Therefore, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}\int 8\operatorname{cosh}⁡t\,\text{d}t=8\int \operatorname{cosh}⁡t\,\text{d}t=8\operatorname{sinh}⁡t+C.\end{aligned}
$$

