Recall that

$$
\dfrac{\textrm d}{\textrm d x}(\sech x) = -\sech{x}\tanh x 
\quad\Rightarrow\quad  
\int \sech{x}\tanh{x} \, \textrm dx = -\sech{x} + C.
$$

Therefore, we have

$$
\begin{aligned}\int (-3\operatorname{sech}⁡x\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\,\text{d}x & =-3\int \operatorname{sech}⁡x\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\,\text{d}x \\  & =-3(-\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+C \\  & =3\operatorname{sech}⁡x+C.\end{aligned}
$$

